                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "3. Procedural fairness — the tribunal must engage with any plausible explanation the applicant offers for an apparent inconsistency. Where the explanation is not inherently unlikely, it should be accepted unless there is a separately articulated reason to reject it.\n\n4. Holistic assessment — credibility findings must be made in context: cultural background, passage of time, documented trauma, and the manner of interpretation are all relevant inputs.\n\n5. Duty to give reasons — the decision-maker must engage with the substance of the applicant's explanation, not merely note it; a perfunctory dismissal can amount to jurisdictional error reviewable under s 476.",
