                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Gemini Pro conflates evidentiary corroboration with the threshold credibility question. Under common-law procedural fairness principles, the tribunal must engage with the applicant's plausible explanation — not require corroboration as a precondition to accepting it. This conflation risks shifting the burden in a way that defeats Kioa v West principles.",
